;
; Kernel arguments: the command line the stub hands the kernel.
; Normative source: ADR 0041 (docs/decisions/0041-boot-abi.md), rule 5.
; The rules below are copied verbatim from that record. SP, DIGIT and
; DQUOTE are the RFC 5234 core rules.
;
; Rule 5 also limits the line to 4096 bytes. The grammar does not
; express that limit; parsers enforce it separately.
; Test vectors: kernel-args.vectors.

kernel-args = *SP [ arg *( 1*SP arg ) *SP ]
arg         = key [ "=" value ]
key         = segment *( "." segment )
segment     = lower *( lower / DIGIT / "-" )
lower       = %x61-7A
value       = bare / quoted
bare        = 1*bare-char
bare-char   = %x21 / %x23-7E                ; printable, not SP or DQUOTE
quoted      = DQUOTE *( q-char / escape ) DQUOTE
q-char      = %x20-21 / %x23-5B / %x5D-7E   ; not DQUOTE or "\"
escape      = "\" ( DQUOTE / "\" )
